{"name":"Artist’s Shadow","hex":"#a1969b","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"artist","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A person who creates art.\nA person who creates art as an occupation.","A person who creates art as an occupation."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Artistic."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/artist"},{"term":"shadow","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A dark image projected onto a surface where light (or other radiation) is blocked by the shade of an object.","Relative darkness, especially as caused by the interruption of light; gloom; obscurity."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Unofficial, informal, unauthorized, but acting as though it were.","Having power or influence, but not widely known or recognized."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shadow"}],"entries":[{"title":"Shadow","blocks":[{"text":"A shadow is a dark area on a surface where light from a light source is blocked by an object. In contrast, shade occupies the three-dimensional volume behind an object with light in front of it. The cross-section of a shadow is a two-dimensional silhouette, or a reverse projection of the object blocking the light."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ef/The_shadow_of_a_musician_playing_transverse_flute.jpg/330px-The_shadow_of_a_musician_playing_transverse_flute.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shadow","wikidata":"Q160020"},{"title":"Artist","blocks":[{"text":"An artist is a person who creates art or practices the arts. The most common usage in everyday speech and academic discourse refers to a practitioner of the visual arts, such as painting or drawing."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/85/Artists_Collage.png/330px-Artists_Collage.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia